      "file": "libyara/compiler.c",
      "function": "yr_compiler_add_string",
      "line": 576,
      "code": "return yr_lex_parse_rules_string(rules_string, compiler);",
      "note": "After the fuzzer buffer is copied into a NUL-terminated string, YARA forwards it directly into the rule lexer/parser. No container/header parsing intervenes before the vulnerable token lifetime path.",
      "oracle_kind": "gt_parser_checkpoint",
      "kind": "parser_admitted"
    },
    {
      "file": "libyara/lexer.l",
      "function": "yara_yylex",
      "line": 402,
      "code": "yylval->c_string = yr_strdup(yytext);",
      "note": "Source. The first byte of the PoC, `F`, matches the identifier rule and is duplicated into a heap string stored in the semantic value for token `_IDENTIFIER_`. ASan reports this allocation as a 2-byte region allocated by `__strdup` from `yara_yylex`.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "libyara/grammar.c",
      "function": "yydestruct",
      "line": null,
      "code": "yr_free(((*yyvaluep).c_string));",
      "note": "Root cause. The `_IDENTIFIER_` destructor frees the token-owned string but does not clear the `YYSTYPE` slot afterwards. The dangling pointer remains in the union and is later reinterpreted as a `_REGEXP_` `sized_string` pointer. The fix changes this destructor (and the analogous token destructors) to assign the field to `NULL` immediately after `yr_free`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "libyara/grammar.c",
      "function": "yydestruct",
      "line": 1346,
      "code": "yr_free(((*yyvaluep).c_string));",
      "note": "Root cause. The `_IDENTIFIER_` destructor frees the token-owned string but does not clear the `YYSTYPE` slot afterwards. The dangling pointer remains in the union and is later reinterpreted as a `_REGEXP_` `sized_string` pointer. The fix changes this destructor (and the analogous token destructors) to assign the field to `NULL` immediately after `yr_free`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_line"
    },
    {
      "file": "libyara/grammar.c",
      "function": "yara_yyparse",
      "line": null,
      "code": "yydestruct (\"Error: discarding\", yytoken, &yylval, yyscanner, compiler);",
      "note": "Sink. While still in parser error recovery, `yyparse` discards the empty `_REGEXP_` lookahead. Its `%destructor` case frees `yyvaluep->sized_string`, but that union field still contains the stale identifier pointer from the first discard, so the same heap region is freed a second time. The saved ASan trace reports both the previous free and the crashing free from this `grammar.c:3868` discard path.",
      "kind": "sink_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "libyara/grammar.c",
